Z||000000||gusto||10-07-2001||04:19 AM||||Ok this may be a stupid question, but what motor is in the 85 SE V6. A friend told me he believes its a 350 but he's not sure. Please constructive and helpful replys only, keep your smart ass comments to yourself.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||Flamberge||10-07-2001||04:39 AM||||The V-6 that comes in Fieros are 2.8 liter V-6 engines... hope this helps.<P>- Flamberge||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||10-07-2001||08:35 AM||||Is it a stock motor?  Maybe someone installed a 350.  There were only two stock motors.  The Iron Duke/Tech 4, 2.5 L 4 cyl and the above mentioned 6 banger.<P>Post some pics if it's something other than stock.<P>BTW--I'm doing my best to restrain myself from typing any smart ass answers.  <FONT SIZE="1">I don't want my butt kicked.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||85 gt fiero||10-07-2001||10:00 AM||||Look on the distrubtor, if there are 9 plugs you have a V8 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, if there is only seven you have a stock 2.8 litre V6.   Randy <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000004||WampusCat||10-07-2001||10:02 AM||||Mucho gusto!  Cool, another Memphian.  The 2.8=about 170 cubic inches, or about half the displacement of a 350 V8.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||gusto||10-08-2001||02:14 PM||||Ok I know the stock engine is a 2.8 liter V6, but does that describe the motor? When someone ask me what motor I got what would I say?                                                                                                                                    Thanks for being patient with the mechanically "declined"||||reg||1
